\begin{align*}
\text{GDP} &= \text{C} + \text{I} + \text{G} + \text{NX}\\
&= \text{Consumption} + \text{Investment} + \text{Government Spending} + \text{Net Exports}\\
&= \text{\$10 trillion} + \text{\$2 trillion} + \text{\$3 trillion} + (\text{\$1 trillion} - \text{\$0.5 trillion})\\
&= \text{\$15.5 trillion}
\end{align*}
In this example, the GDP of the country is calculated by adding up the consumption, investment, government spending, and net exports. The values for each of these components are given in trillions of dollars, and the final result is also in trillions of dollars.

