To calculate the distance between two cities in C++ using latitude and longitude values, you can use the Haversine formula. The Haversine formula calculates the great-circle distance between two points on a sphere, such as the Earth, taking into account the non-spherical shape of the Earth.
Here's an example code for calculating the distance between Seattle and Vancouver, and the distance between Boston and New York:
```
#include <iostream>
#include <cmath>
using namespace std;
const double PI = 3.14159265358979323846;
const double EARTH_RADIUS = 6371.0; // in kilometers
double toRadians(double degrees) {
    return degrees * PI / 180.0;
}
double haversine(double lat1, double lon1, double lat2, double lon2) {
    double dLat = toRadians(lat2 - lat1);
    double dLon = toRadians(lon2 - lon1);
    double a = sin(dLat / 2) * sin(dLat / 2) +
               cos(toRadians(lat1)) * cos(toRadians(lat2)) *
               sin(dLon / 2) * sin(dLon / 2);
    double c = 2 * atan2(sqrt(a), sqrt(1 - a));
    return EARTH_RADIUS * c;
}
int main() {
    double seattleLat = 47.6062;
    double seattleLon = -122.3321;
    double vancouverLat = 49.2827;
    double vancouverLon = -123.1207;
    double bostonLat = 42.3601;
    double bostonLon = -71.0589;
    double newYorkLat = 40.7128;
    double newYorkLon = -74.0060;
    double seattleToVancouver = haversine(seattleLat, seattleLon, vancouverLat, vancouverLon);
    double bostonToNewYork = haversine(bostonLat, bostonLon, newYorkLat, newYorkLon);
    cout << "Distance between Seattle and Vancouver: " << seattleToVancouver << " km" << endl;
    cout << "Distance between Boston and New York: " << bostonToNewYork << " km" << endl;
    return 0;
}
```
This code defines the `toRadians` function to convert degrees to radians, and the `haversine` function to calculate the distance between two points using the Haversine formula. The `main` function uses the `haversine` function to calculate the distance between Seattle and Vancouver, and the distance between Boston and New York, and prints the results to the console.
Note that the latitude and longitude values used in this example are approximate.

