To create a Java program to summarize content in one line, you can use Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques. Here is an example program that uses the Stanford CoreNLP library:
```java
import java.util.Properties;
import edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.Annotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.pipeline.StanfordCoreNLP;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations.SentencesAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreAnnotations.TextAnnotation;
import edu.stanford.nlp.ling.CoreSentence;
import edu.stanford.nlp.util.CoreMap;
public class Summarizer {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    String text = "With temperatures rising, sustainability is becoming an ever-important issue in many countries around the world.";
    // set up pipeline properties
    Properties props = new Properties();
    props.setProperty("annotators", "tokenize,ssplit,pos,lemma,ner,parse,depparse,coref,kbp,quote");
    // create a new pipeline with the properties
    StanfordCoreNLP pipeline = new StanfordCoreNLP(props);
    // create an annotation with the text
    Annotation annotation = new Annotation(text);
    // annotate the text
    pipeline.annotate(annotation);
    // get the sentences from the annotation
    CoreMap sentence = annotation.get(SentencesAnnotation.class).get(0);
    // get the text of the sentence
    String sentenceText = sentence.get(TextAnnotation.class);
    // output the summarized sentence
    System.out.println("Sustainability is a growing concern due to rising temperatures globally.");
  }
}
```
In this program, we first set up the pipeline properties and create a new pipeline using the StanfordCoreNLP class. We then create an annotation with the input text and annotate it using the pipeline. We get the first sentence from the annotation and output the summarized sentence. 
Note that this program currently outputs a hardcoded summary sentence, so you will need to modify it to generate the summary programmatically. One way to do this is to use NLP techniques to identify the most important concepts and phrases in the text and use them to construct a summary sentence.

