```csharp
public static void GenerateChessboard(int size, string orientation)
{
    string[,] chessboard = new string[size, size];
    // Fill the chessboard with alternating black and white squares
    for (int row = 0; row < size; row++)
    {
        for (int col = 0; col < size; col++)
        {
            if ((row + col) % 2 == 0)
            {
                chessboard[row, col] = "W";
            }
            else
            {
                chessboard[row, col] = "B";
            }
        }
    }
    // Print the chessboard based on the specified orientation
    if (orientation.ToLower() == "horizontal")
    {
        for (int row = 0; row < size; row++)
        {
            for (int col = 0; col < size; col++)
            {
                Console.Write(chessboard[row, col] + " ");
            }
            Console.WriteLine();
        }
    }
    else if (orientation.ToLower() == "vertical")
    {
        for (int col = 0; col < size; col++)
        {
            for (int row = 0; row < size; row++)
            {
                Console.Write(chessboard[row, col] + " ");
            }
            Console.WriteLine();
        }
    }
    else
    {
        Console.WriteLine("Invalid orientation specified.");
    }
}
```
This function first creates a 2D array to represent the chessboard, with the specified size. It then uses nested loops to fill the chessboard with alternating black and white squares, based on the row and column indices. 
Finally, the function prints the chessboard based on the specified orientation. If the orientation is "horizontal", it simply prints each row of the chessboard. If the orientation is "vertical", it prints each column of the chessboard. If an invalid orientation is specified, the function prints an error message.
To use this function, you can call it with the desired size and orientation, like this:
```csharp
GenerateChessboard(8, "horizontal");
```
This would generate an 8x8 chessboard with a horizontal orientation.

