5. The `binarySearch` method takes in the array and target element as parameters.
6. We initialize two variables `left` and `right` to represent the left and right indices of the array.
7. We use a `while` loop to repeatedly search for the target element in the array.
8. We calculate the middle index of the array using the formula `mid = left + (right - left) / 2`.
9. If the middle element is equal to the target element, we return the index of the middle element.
10. If the middle element is less than the target element, we update the `left` index to be `mid + 1`.
11. If the middle element is greater than the target element, we update the `right` index to be `mid - 1`.
